#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tvbox-monitor - visibility and integrity monitor for TV boxes on a local LAN.

What it can see (honest scope)
------------------------------
On a switched LAN where this host is not the gateway, only L2 broadcast and
multicast are visible: ARP, DHCP, SSDP/UPnP, mDNS, NBNS/LLMNR and IPv6 ND/RA.
Unicast traffic between a TV box and the router (streaming, HTTPS, QUIC, DNS)
is NOT visible from here.

What it actually detects
------------------------
  * inventory drift: new devices, IP/MAC changes, vendor/hostname changes
  * exposed services: ADB (5555), telnet (23), SMB, VNC, RDP, web UIs
  * L2 integrity attacks: gateway ARP conflict, duplicate IP claimants,
    rogue DHCP servers, rogue IPv6 router advertisements, ARP storms
  * device behaviour: SSDP M-SEARCH/NOTIFY bursts, DHCP fingerprints,
    mDNS service names, UPnP device descriptors (make/model)
  * optional: DNS query log analysis when devices use this host as resolver

It never changes network state, never ARP-spoofs and never MITMs anything.

Usage
-----
  tvbox-monitor discover            # ARP sweep + fingerprint + diff vs baseline
  tvbox-monitor devices             # current inventory
  tvbox-monitor report --hours 24   # findings + integrity summary
  sudo tvbox-monitor watch          # continuous sniffer + periodic rescans
  tvbox-monitor probe 192.168.1.43  # deep dive on one host
  tvbox-monitor trust <mac|ip>      # mark as known/good

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 3 findings at/above --fail-on severity.
"""

